adjudication.rationale:
The diff changes the catch block in `EventManager.ts` `updateCalendarRefs` to:

```ts
return Promise.resolve(
  calendarReference?.map((reference) => ({ ...success:false... })) ?? ([] as Array<EventResult<...>>)
);
```

If an exception is thrown before `calendarReference` is set (it’s initialized as `undefined` at the top of the function), this will now return `[]`, whereas the previous code always returned an array containing at least one `{ success: false, ... }` result. That can silently swallow/report no failures to the caller in error scenarios when `calendarReference` is undefined, matching the finding.

In `packages/core/EventManager.ts`, the diff changes `destinationCalendar` to an array and adds:

```ts
const [mainHostDestinationCalendar] = evt.destinationCalendar ?? [];
if (evt.location === MeetLocationType && mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration !== "google_calendar") {
  ...
}
```

If `evt.destinationCalendar` is `null`, `undefined`, or an empty array, `mainHostDestinationCalendar` will be `undefined`, and accessing `mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration` will throw a `TypeError`. This is a concrete crash path introduced by the diff when `evt.location` is Google Meet.
